<mujoco model="loop_corridor">
    <!--
    Closed rectangular-ring corridor, built for visually evaluating
    examples/run_racecar_core.py's --viewer path against a wall-following
    controller (e.g. examples/ultimate_wall_follower/wall_follower.py).

    straight_corridor.xml is a dead end: a controller running its full-speed,
    untouched config exits the far end in ~1-2s of sim time, well before any
    steady-state wall-following behavior (oscillation, cornering stability,
    sustained wall distance) is visible. This track instead loops back on
    itself, so a working controller can drive it indefinitely with no walls
    ever running out.

    This is scenery ONLY — it does not name the car. The runner attaches
    neoracer.xml at runtime (same MjSpec.attach_body pattern as
    straight_corridor.xml / ramp_course.xml), so this scene stays independent
    of the car model.

    Layout (top-down, +X = forward, +Y = left). Outer wall is an 8m x 6m
    rectangle (x:[-4,4], y:[-3,3]); inner wall is a 6m x 4m rectangle
    (x:[-3,3], y:[-2,2]); the corridor between them is a uniform 1.0 m wide
    ring on the straights (same width as straight_corridor.xml, for the same
    reason: wide relative to the car's 0.235 m track, so the controller has
    real room to wander and correct rather than being pinned centered by
    geometry alone).

    Corners are 45-degree CHAMFERED, not square: a first version of this
    track had plain 90-degree corners, and the wall-following controller
    (config/wall_follower.yaml's untouched speed=1.0) reliably clipped the
    outer wall approaching the very first corner and tumbled -- not a lack
    of collision handling, a genuine "this controller can't make this corner
    at this speed with zero reaction room" failure. Each corner instead cuts
    a 1.0 m chamfer off both the inner and outer walls, which (a) turns one
    90-degree direction change into two gentler ~45-degree ones with a wider
    bay in between (the diagonal-to-diagonal distance across a chamfered
    corner is ~1.41 m, wider than the 1.0 m straights), and (b) delays where
    the outer wall closes in ahead of the car, giving the controller's
    forward-clearance probe more room to react before the turn.

        +Y  ┌───────────────╲       ╱───────────────┐   outer (y=+3)
            │                ╲     ╱                │
            │     ┌───────────╲   ╱───────────┐     │   inner (y=+2)
            │     │                            │     │
            │     │      car → (x=0,y=-2.5)    │     │
            │     └───────────╱   ╲───────────┘     │   inner (y=-2)
            │                ╱     ╲                │
         -Y └───────────────╱       ╲───────────────┘   outer (y=-3)
              x=-4                                 x=4

    The car spawns centered in the bottom straight segment (y=-2.5, midway
    between the inner and outer bottom walls), facing +X -- same
    "car spawns already centered, facing down a straight" convention as
    straight_corridor.xml. Because the wall-following controller centers
    between whichever two walls it currently sees (not "always follow the
    right/left wall specifically"), the loop works the same way whichever
    direction the car ends up circling.

    Ground plane: neoracer.xml's own floor geom is NOT pulled in by
    attach_body (see straight_corridor.xml's docstring for why), so this
    track carries its own floor, sized to cover the full outer rectangle
    plus margin.
    -->

    <asset>
        <texture name="loop_grid" type="2d" builtin="checker" width="512" height="512"
                 rgb1=".1 .2 .3" rgb2=".2 .3 .4"/>
        <material name="loop_floor" texture="loop_grid" texrepeat="4 4" texuniform="true"
                  reflectance=".2"/>
        <material name="wall" rgba=".55 .57 .60 1"/>
    </asset>

    <default>
        <default class="scenery">
            <geom type="box" material="wall" condim="3" friction="1.0 0.1 0.1"/>
        </default>
    </default>

    <worldbody>
        <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="4.5 3.9 .01" pos="0 0 0"
              material="loop_floor" friction="1.5 0.1 0.1"/>

        <!-- outer ring (8m x 6m outer footprint): each straight wall is cut
             1.0m short of the corner on both ends (a 0.05m overlap is added
             back in so it still seals against the diagonal chamfer piece
             below -- 3.0+0.05, 2.0+0.05). -->
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_top"    pos="0  3 .15" size="3.05 .02 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_bottom" pos="0 -3 .15" size="3.05 .02 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_left"   pos="-4 0 .15" size=".02 2.05 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_right"  pos=" 4 0 .15" size=".02 2.05 .15"/>

        <!-- outer corner chamfers: each connects the shortened outer_top/
             outer_bottom endpoint to the shortened outer_left/outer_right
             endpoint with a 45-degree diagonal (e.g. top-right runs from
             (3,3) to (4,2)). 0.757 = 1.0m corner cut's diagonal half-length
             (0.5*sqrt(2)) plus the same 0.05m overlap. -->
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_chamfer_tr" pos=" 3.5  2.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0 -45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_chamfer_tl" pos="-3.5  2.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0  45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_chamfer_br" pos=" 3.5 -2.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0  45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="outer_chamfer_bl" pos="-3.5 -2.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0 -45"/>

        <!-- inner ring (6m x 4m outer footprint of the inner wall): same
             1.0m-short-plus-overlap construction, chamfering the corners
             that would otherwise poke into the turn. -->
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_top"    pos="0  2 .15" size="2.05 .02 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_bottom" pos="0 -2 .15" size="2.05 .02 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_left"   pos="-3 0 .15" size=".02 1.05 .15"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_right"  pos=" 3 0 .15" size=".02 1.05 .15"/>

        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_chamfer_tr" pos=" 2.5  1.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0 -45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_chamfer_tl" pos="-2.5  1.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0  45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_chamfer_br" pos=" 2.5 -1.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0  45"/>
        <geom class="scenery" name="inner_chamfer_bl" pos="-2.5 -1.5 .15" size=".757 .02 .15" euler="0 0 -45"/>
    </worldbody>
</mujoco>
